<p>On April 23, 2001, Marcelo Nicchio appeared in the <strong>cover story of Folhateen</strong>, the youth supplement of <em>Folha de S.Paulo</em>, published after Joey Ramone's death. The printed cover line was <strong>“Órfãos do Rock”</strong> (“Orphans of Rock”); the inside article preserved in Folha's official digital archive was titled <strong>“Onde estão os ídolos?”</strong> (“Where are the idols?”).</p>
<p>The article records his comments on Joey Ramone, punk culture, the do-it-yourself principle, the Brazilian underground market and the persistence of rock.</p>
